{"id":"u-1bfd6bd0-79ac-46c3-826f-31f294d811ad","src":"community","title":"The Hourglass Protocol ⏳(the 45 min reshape!)","author":"Sedalia C.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/BuxyRj-sedalias-deluxe-workout-program","desc":"The point of this plan is to change your shape: a smaller-looking waist, fuller glutes, and less body fat overall. It does that with short, mostly free-weight sessions you can run at almost any gym.\n\nFirst, the thing nobody likes to hear: you can't choose where your body loses fat. There's no move that trims the waist or the thighs specifically, and your fat-loss pattern is mostly genetics. So we don't fight that. We work two angles instead:\n\n➡️ The first angle is building the muscles that make your waist look smaller. Wider lats and capped rear delts up top, rounder glutes down below, and suddenly your waist looks narrower next to them, even before the tape changes. \n➡️ The second angle is dropping body fat, which comes from hard training plus how you eat. That's just where fat loss actually happens.\n\nThese are each about 45 minutes and nothing in here is filler. The big free-weight lifts (hip thrusts, RDLs, rows, presses) are doing most of the work because they hit the muscles that matter for your goal and they burn more than picking off one muscle at a time on a machine. Pairing exercises back to back keeps your heart rate up, which is how we cover for the cardio you'd rather skip. And the ab work is built to pull your middle in tight and flat, not to thicken your obliques, which is why you won't see me loading up heavy side bends.\n\nWhat makes all of this work over time is simple: get stronger. Stay in the rep ranges, add weight when you can, and document it here. If your numbers are going up week to week, your body is changing too. That's also your proof the plan is doing its job.\n\nYou don't need a scale for any of this, and you're better off without one right now. A tape measure on your waist, hips, and thighs, a monthly photo, and how your jeans fit will tell you more. The scale can sit still while you're losing fat and gaining muscle, which just messes with your head.\n\nLast thing: this plan moves with you. Every exercise has a swap, free weight or machine, so when you switch gyms you just grab whatever's there and keep going. The plan doesn't change, only the equipment does.\n\nSo the whole idea is this: Build up your shoulders, back, and glutes, keep the training hard and quick, eat in a way that supports it, and watch the right things instead of the scale. Do that and the waistline takes care of itself.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Women's","Strength","Athletics"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":40,"joins":7,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-11-02T13:24:29.322Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Lower A — Glutes & Hamstrings","Upper A — Back & Shoulders","Lower B — Legs & Glute Balance","Upper B — Push / Pull & Arms"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Hip Thrust (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hip Abductor (Machine)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":2}]},{"n":"Hanging Knee Raise","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":10,"x":4}],"note":"Wide/neutral grip"},{"n":"Seated Row (Machine)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pallof Press","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hip Thrust (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Reverse Lunge (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hip Abductor (Machine)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Calf Raise","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Dead Bug","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"L